&lt;li&gt;Engage actively with government-led AI initiatives, including participation in forums like the India AI Impact Summit and state-level AI conferences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute innovative sales strategies tailored to the Indian public sector environment, meeting and exceeding revenue targets while maintaining strong relationships with procurement teams and decision-makers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide market intelligence and feedback to product teams to ensure our offerings meet Indian public sector requirements, use cases, and regulatory considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships with relevant systems integrators (including TCS, Infosys, Wipro), technology partners, and government digital transformation partners in the Indian market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and document best practices for Indian public sector engagement, creating playbooks that can scale our presence in the market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a leader within the broader public sector team, sharing insights and collaborating on cross-market opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of enterprise sales experience in the Indian public sector, with a proven track record of driving adoption of emerging technologies across central and state government departments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of Indian government procurement processes (including GeM, tender processes), security requirements, and technology adoption frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating India&#39;s regulatory environment, including data localization requirements, IT Act compliance, and emerging AI governance frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build and grow new market segments, with potential to develop into a leadership role as our India operations scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of managing complex sales cycles and securing strategic deals in the public sector, with experience in both central and state government engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating multiple stakeholders across government departments and ministries, building consensus and providing innovative solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and ability to present confidently to all levels, from technical teams to senior government officials and secretaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinking combined with hands-on execution capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while maintaining strong collaboration with global teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a dynamic, high-growth environment with evolving regulatory frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for safe and ethical AI development, with the ability to articulate its importance in the public sector context, particularly for inclusive development and governance transformation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English required; proficiency in Hindi or other regional languages is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Delhi, India&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
