&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of Anthropic&#39;s Global Safety, Intelligence, and Security (GSIS) team, the NYC Campus Security Manager serves as the operational security leader for Anthropic&#39;s New York City campuses. This position offers the opportunity to lead comprehensive security operations protecting cutting-edge AI research while building trust and security culture with Anthropic personnel. You&#39;ll serve as an approachable security partner who fosters open communication, oversees vendor performance, leads incident response, and coordinates cross-functional security initiatives that enable rather than restrict productivity. Working collaboratively with the greater Security Operations team, you&#39;ll balance hands-on operational leadership with strategic input on security planning while ensuring robust security posture across all NYC locations and maintaining AI Safety Level (ASL) compliance requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Campus Security Operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead comprehensive security operations for NYC-based campuses, ensuring safety, security, and well-being of all employees, visitors, and assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Culture &amp;amp; Trust Building:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as approachable security partner who builds trust with Anthropic personnel, fostering open communication and integrating security practices into daily operations without creating barriers to productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Planning:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and implement security strategies for NYC campus that align with Anthropic&#39;s growth and evolving threat landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Train and coordinate security personnel and vendors, fostering culture of professionalism and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emergency Response:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead and coordinate emergency response efforts for NYC campus, ensuring rapid and effective reactions to fires, medical emergencies, or security breaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community Relations:&lt;/strong&gt; Build strong relationships with New York City Police Department, local emergency services, and community leaders to enhance campus security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Access Control:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Access Risk Management on administration of access control systems, managing permissions and auditing access logs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Technology:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with IT and cross-functional teams to integrate and optimize campus security technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Project Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage security aspects of office remediations, process improvements, and new real estate needs, contributing strategic security requirements for NYC campus development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You may be a good fit if you:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a passion for creating safe, secure environments that foster productivity and well-being&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess strong leadership skills and have experience coordinating security teams and vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are adept at building relationships with various stakeholders, including law enforcement and community leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have excellent crisis management skills and can lead effectively under pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are knowledgeable about physical security technologies and their applications in campus settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are an effective communicator, able to convey security concepts to a wide audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 8+ years of progressive experience in security operations leadership or campus security management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in or willing to relocate to New York City with ability to work on-site full-time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable supporting operations that may require a flexible schedule including 24/7 on-call rotation and after-hours response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Strong candidates may have:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience securing high-profile or high-risk campus environments in technology or research sectors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional security certifications such as CPP (Certified Protection Professional) or PSP (Physical Security Professional)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Security Management, Criminal Justice, Emergency Management, or related fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in technology company security operations or R&amp;amp;D facility security management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in law enforcement, military, or executive protection with transition to corporate security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
