&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively with outside counsel, providing clear direction while leveraging their specialized expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills that translate technical infrastructure concepts into clear risk assessments for our business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine interest in compute infrastructure and appreciation for why capacity access is mission-critical for frontier AI development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house experience at datacenter providers or network infrastructure companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background at large technology companies with significant datacenter or colocation footprints supporting facilities and network procurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Law firm experience at practices with infrastructure or telecom specialization, or regional firms with strong utilities/telecom work&lt;/li&gt;
