&lt;h3&gt;Process Improvement &amp;amp; Transformation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify opportunities to streamline and connect processes within and beyond our team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map processes end to end to see how things currently run, find where they break or slow down, and propose solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build improved processes yourself, or document the requirements and partner with technical teams to build them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve cross-functional processes by partnering with other People teams and teams across the org (IT, Security, Legal, Finance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage our employee support experience, focusing on improving our tooling and analyzing data to drive continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect feedback from employees and partner teams to make sure we are focusing on areas that drive the most impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Data Integrity &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage automated processes to audit and maintain the quality of our workforce data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal and external audits with process documentation and evidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document runbooks and SOPs for our processes and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You might be a good fit if you:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 6–10+ years in People/HR Operations and have scaled People Ops functions in-house&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have hands-on experience converting manual processes into scalable systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn systems quickly and enjoy figuring out how things work under the hood&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly with business and technical teams, flexing your communication style for your audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Form strong cross-functional partnerships to collaborate on processes with upstream/downstream impacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Move quickly without sacrificing quality or introducing risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have managed processes and data in enterprise HR systems (e.g. Workday) — configuration experience isn&#39;t necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have managed employee support through ticketing systems (e.g. Jira)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
