&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Procurement Business Partner to serve as Anthropic&#39;s procurement lead for all EMEA purchasing operations. This generalist role will own end-to-end procurement across EMEA markets with particular depth in Real Estate &amp;amp; Workplace and Professional Services categories. You will be the go-to procurement partner for EMEA business stakeholders, building procurement infrastructure and vendor relationships outside the US as Anthropic scales globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires someone who can operate independently across time zones, navigate EMEA contracting complexities, and bring strategic sourcing rigour to a high-growth environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;International Procurement Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end procurement operations for all EMEA purchasing, from intake and sourcing through negotiation, contracting, and ongoing vendor management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary procurement point of contact for EMEA offices, ensuring consistent procurement practices and compliance across geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendor onboarding, purchase requisitions, contract management, and spend analysis for EMEA spend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate EMEA contracting requirements including local regulatory compliance, currency considerations, tax implications, and cross-border vendor structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion Zip adoption and compliance for EMEA business partners; drive workflow improvements and self-service enablement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure PO hygiene, timely receipting, and clean metadata that supports invoice matching, reporting, and financial controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support month-end close activities including accrual submissions and PO reconciliation for EMEA spend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Sourcing &amp;amp; Category Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead strategic sourcing initiatives across EMEA categories with particular focus on Real Estate &amp;amp; Workplace (office buildouts, facilities management, FF&amp;amp;E) and Professional Services (Big 4 advisory, audit, consulting, legal services)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute category strategies that balance cost optimisation, quality, and local market dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct market intelligence and benchmarking across EMEA markets to inform sourcing decisions and ensure competitive pricing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex vendor negotiations independently, structuring deals that account for local market conditions while protecting Anthropic&#39;s financial interests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain preferred-vendor frameworks for key EMEA categories, driving consolidation and leverage where appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage RFP processes for major EMEA engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Partnership &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the embedded procurement partner to EMEA teams across Workplace, Finance, Legal, People, and other functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal, Security, TPRM, and Finance to ensure EMEA vendor engagements meet compliance and risk requirements across jurisdictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex sourcing and financial concepts for non-procurement stakeholders; build trust through responsiveness and results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively surface risks, savings opportunities, and vendor performance insights to business owners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the US-based Procurement team to ensure alignment on global vendor strategies and procurement standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop procurement documentation, training materials, and best practice guides tailored to EMEA operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 7-10 years in procurement operations, strategic sourcing, or category management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;International Procurement:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated experience managing procurement across multiple geographies and navigating EMEA contracting, compliance, and vendor structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Category Depth:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience in at least one of the following: Real Estate &amp;amp; Workplace procurement or Professional Services (Big 4 consulting, advisory, audit, legal)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with Zip, NetSuite, Coupa, or similar procurement platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Negotiation:&lt;/strong&gt; Track record of independently leading complex vendor negotiations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong skills in Excel/Google Sheets; experience with basic SQL or BI tools (Looker, Tableau, Power BI) for vendor and spend analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent written and verbal communication skills; ability to work effectively across time zones and cultural contexts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk &amp;amp; Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Understanding of financial controls, vendor risk management, and procurement compliance requirements in EMEA contexts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ideal Candidate Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generalist mindset with strategic sourcing depth; comfortable spanning multiple categories while going deep on key ones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business partner first, not a gatekeeper; enables speed while maintaining appropriate controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter who can build procurement infrastructure and processes in new markets without a complete playbook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating independently across time zones with a distributed team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High accountability, low ego; builds trust through follow-through and results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brings intellectual curiosity about how procurement enables a mission-driven AI company&#39;s global expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence and ability to influence stakeholders at all levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in technology or AI/ML companies&lt;/li&gt;
